1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,737
Read out roll number twelve
from the class register.

2
00:00:03,737 --> 00:00:05,483
You get exactly one name.

3
00:00:05,483 --> 00:00:07,927
Never two names, and never no name.

4
00:00:08,327 --> 00:00:11,110
Now ask the blood group
list: who is group O?

5
00:00:11,110 --> 00:00:13,623
You might get two names, or none at all.

6
00:00:14,073 --> 00:00:17,075
Aarav noticed this while
his teacher took attendance.

7
00:00:17,425 --> 00:00:21,482
Why does one list always give a single
answer, while the other does not?

8
00:00:21,982 --> 00:00:26,186
Because the register is a function:
a relation with one strict promise.

9
00:00:26,836 --> 00:00:32,281
In NCERT words: a relation f from a
set A to a set B is a function if every

10
00:00:32,281 --> 00:00:35,695
element of A has one
and only one image in B.

11
00:00:36,095 --> 00:00:37,730
So there are two checks.

12
00:00:37,730 --> 00:00:40,663
First, every element of
A must have an image.

13
00:00:40,663 --> 00:00:42,971
No element is left without an arrow.

14
00:00:43,371 --> 00:00:46,576
Second, each element of
A has only one image.

15
00:00:46,576 --> 00:00:48,832
No element sends out two arrows.

16
00:00:49,482 --> 00:00:53,286
Let us run the function test
on three relations from A to B.

17
00:00:53,636 --> 00:00:54,853
The first one.

18
00:00:54,853 --> 00:00:56,296
One goes to four.

19
00:00:56,296 --> 00:00:57,740
Two goes to five.

20
00:00:57,740 --> 00:00:59,625
Three also goes to five.

21
00:00:59,625 --> 00:01:02,275
Each element sends exactly one arrow.

22
00:01:02,275 --> 00:01:03,212
It passes.

23
00:01:03,212 --> 00:01:04,655
It is a function.

24
00:01:05,055 --> 00:01:06,255
The second one.

25
00:01:06,255 --> 00:01:09,243
One sends two arrows, to four and to six.

26
00:01:09,243 --> 00:01:11,063
One element, two images.

27
00:01:11,063 --> 00:01:11,963
It fails.

28
00:01:12,296 --> 00:01:13,468
The third one.

29
00:01:13,468 --> 00:01:15,449
Two sends no arrow at all.

30
00:01:15,449 --> 00:01:17,316
An element with no image.

31
00:01:17,316 --> 00:01:18,436
It fails too.

32
00:01:19,086 --> 00:01:21,074
There is a grid picture as well.

33
00:01:21,074 --> 00:01:23,746
Put A along the bottom, and B up the side.

34
00:01:23,746 --> 00:01:25,060
Each pair is a dot.

35
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:28,630
A function puts exactly
one dot in every column.

36
00:01:28,630 --> 00:01:33,400
Two dots in one column, or an empty
column, and it is not a function.

37
00:01:34,050 --> 00:01:35,125
Side by side.

38
00:01:35,125 --> 00:01:38,617
Many arrows out of one
element of A are not allowed.

39
00:01:38,617 --> 00:01:40,966
That element would have two images.

40
00:01:41,366 --> 00:01:44,316
But many arrows into one
element of B are fine.

41
00:01:44,316 --> 00:01:48,547
In the first test, one and two point
to different numbers, but two and

42
00:01:48,547 --> 00:01:50,299
three share the image five.

43
00:01:50,299 --> 00:01:51,479
Still a function.

44
00:01:52,079 --> 00:01:53,027
Now you try.

45
00:01:53,027 --> 00:01:55,772
Every student is linked
to their birth month.

46
00:01:55,772 --> 00:01:57,521
Two students share a month.

47
00:01:57,521 --> 00:01:59,087
Is it still a function?

48
00:01:59,087 --> 00:02:00,220
Pause and think.

49
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:04,320
Yes!

50
00:02:03,905 --> 00:02:06,836
Each student still has
exactly one birth month.

51
00:02:06,836 --> 00:02:08,692
Sharing an image is allowed.

52
00:02:08,692 --> 00:02:12,412
Only a student with two months,
or none, would break it.

53
00:02:13,062 --> 00:02:14,115
Remember this.

54
00:02:14,115 --> 00:02:17,962
In a function, every element
of A sends exactly one arrow.

55
00:02:18,662 --> 00:02:20,955
Functions have their own way of writing.

56
00:02:21,305 --> 00:02:23,269
We write f colon A arrow B.

57
00:02:23,269 --> 00:02:26,042
It reads: f is a function from A to B.

58
00:02:26,442 --> 00:02:29,980
If a comma b is in f, we
write f of a equals b.

59
00:02:29,980 --> 00:02:34,338
Here b is the image of a under
f, and a is the preimage of b.

60
00:02:34,988 --> 00:02:38,239
Now, how many functions
can we make from A to B?

61
00:02:38,239 --> 00:02:41,929
This counting is not in the
NCERT text, but JEE asks it.

62
00:02:42,279 --> 00:02:43,179
Step one.

63
00:02:43,106 --> 00:02:46,232
Say A has p elements,
and B has q elements.

64
00:02:46,982 --> 00:02:47,882
Step two.

65
00:02:47,856 --> 00:02:51,149
Each element of A must
pick exactly one image.

66
00:02:51,149 --> 00:02:52,577
It has q choices.

67
00:02:53,327 --> 00:02:54,239
Step three.

68
00:02:54,239 --> 00:02:58,067
The choices are made one after
another, and each is free.

69
00:02:58,067 --> 00:02:59,693
So the counts multiply.

70
00:03:00,443 --> 00:03:01,343
Step four.

71
00:03:01,313 --> 00:03:04,624
q times q times q, once
for each element of A.

72
00:03:04,624 --> 00:03:07,105
That is q to the power p functions.

73
00:03:07,755 --> 00:03:09,490
Now, one worked example.

74
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:11,517
A is one, two, three.

75
00:03:11,517 --> 00:03:13,669
B is four, five, six, seven.

76
00:03:13,669 --> 00:03:17,898
Is f, with one to four, two to
six, three to six, a function?

77
00:03:17,898 --> 00:03:19,007
Find f of two.

78
00:03:19,507 --> 00:03:20,407
Step one.

79
00:03:20,297 --> 00:03:23,312
List the first elements:
one, two and three.

80
00:03:23,312 --> 00:03:25,143
Every element of A appears.

81
00:03:25,893 --> 00:03:26,793
Step two.

82
00:03:26,761 --> 00:03:29,364
Each first element appears only once.

83
00:03:29,364 --> 00:03:31,598
So each element has one image.

84
00:03:32,348 --> 00:03:33,248
Step three.

85
00:03:33,224 --> 00:03:35,480
Two and three share the image six.

86
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:36,651
That is allowed.

87
00:03:37,401 --> 00:03:38,315
Step four.

88
00:03:38,315 --> 00:03:41,688
So f is a function, and
f of two equals six.

89
00:03:42,438 --> 00:03:43,351
Step five.

90
00:03:43,351 --> 00:03:45,669
Five and seven have no preimage.

91
00:03:45,669 --> 00:03:47,232
That is allowed too.

92
00:03:47,232 --> 00:03:49,571
B does not need to be used up.

93
00:03:50,221 --> 00:03:51,684
Now, the exam trap.

94
00:03:52,034 --> 00:03:56,907
Many students say f is not a function
because five and seven in B get no

95
00:03:56,907 --> 00:03:57,807
arrows.

96
00:03:58,004 --> 00:04:00,776
But the rule only checks
the elements of A.

97
00:04:00,776 --> 00:04:04,717
Every element of A has exactly
one image, so f is a function.

98
00:04:05,367 --> 00:04:06,751
Where is this asked?

99
00:04:06,751 --> 00:04:10,520
In JEE Main, as: count the
functions that obey a condition.

100
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:12,291
Exam level now.

101
00:04:12,291 --> 00:04:14,077
A is one, two, three.

102
00:04:14,077 --> 00:04:16,319
B is one, two, three, four.

103
00:04:16,319 --> 00:04:21,061
How many functions f from A to B
have f of one not equal to f of two?

104
00:04:21,061 --> 00:04:22,281
Pause and solve.

105
00:04:27,681 --> 00:04:29,075
The answer is A.

106
00:04:29,075 --> 00:04:30,124
Forty eight.

107
00:04:30,624 --> 00:04:34,802
With no condition, each of the
three elements has four choices.

108
00:04:34,802 --> 00:04:37,173
Four cubed is sixty four functions.

109
00:04:37,673 --> 00:04:42,121
Now count the ones we do not want,
where f of one equals f of two.

110
00:04:42,621 --> 00:04:47,758
f of one has four choices, f of two
must copy it, and f of three has four

111
00:04:47,758 --> 00:04:48,658
choices.

112
00:04:48,490 --> 00:04:49,759
That is sixteen.

113
00:04:50,259 --> 00:04:53,033
Sixty four minus sixteen
leaves forty eight.

114
00:04:53,633 --> 00:04:55,093
Here is your recap.

115
00:04:55,093 --> 00:04:56,594
Screenshot this card.

116
00:04:59,794 --> 00:05:02,631
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

117
00:05:03,031 --> 00:05:03,931
One.

118
00:05:03,532 --> 00:05:08,192
Is the relation one comma two, one
comma three, two comma four a function

119
00:05:08,192 --> 00:05:10,818
from one, two to two, three, four?

120
00:05:11,718 --> 00:05:12,618
Two.

121
00:05:12,168 --> 00:05:16,286
How many functions are there from a
set of two elements to a set of three

122
00:05:16,286 --> 00:05:17,186
elements?

123
00:05:17,858 --> 00:05:18,758
Three.

124
00:05:18,459 --> 00:05:23,093
If f of three equals seven, which
number is the image, and which is the

125
00:05:23,093 --> 00:05:23,993
preimage?

126
00:05:24,942 --> 00:05:29,648
Next time: marks can be anything
from zero to a hundred, but the class

127
00:05:29,648 --> 00:05:32,180
only scored forty one to ninety six.

128
00:05:32,180 --> 00:05:34,548
That gap is codomain versus range.
